# Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth: "Sacrifice a Clue" is a cost paid from the Clues Bot1 controls (CR 701.21a, 602.2b), and a Clue sacrificed once cannot pay a second cost (the ruling). Bot2's Thraben Inspector makes a Clue on turn 2. On
# turn 3 Bot1, holding Alquist untapped, Black Lotus (UUU) and Mox Pearl (W) with plenty of mana, sacrifices its own Clue to the Clue's own ability ({2} from Mox Sapphire and Mox Jet: it draws): Alquist is then refused
# although the pool could pay X = 0 ({W}{U}{U}), because the only Clue left is Bot2's.

